# Eight controller slots, one per fielder, for network play.
#
# The GameCube had four pad ports, and the game's per-pad state was sized to
# match. A network match gives every fielder on both teams a human: slots 0-3
# are the home captain and three sidekicks, 4-7 the away team's. NL_MAX_PADS
# (8) sizes the pad state, the AI pad table, flick history, the per-player
# swap timers and the rumble state, and the loops over them. Ports 4-7 never
# come from PADRead -- only from the host's agreed network input -- and stay
# unplugged otherwise. The front end still offers four.
#
# Data the memory card saves keeps its four entries: mPadSides comes from the
# host for slots past four (and for all of them in a network match, through
# osHostPadSide), and per-controller stats are not kept for slots past four.
# Rumble goes through osHostControlMotor, which only shakes this machine's own
# controllers. Indicators for slots 4-7 reuse the art of 1-4.
#
# Fielders: each network slot names its fielder (osHostPadFielder), which
# cTeam::UpdateControllers gives it first. A team whose four fielders all have
# a human is locked (osHostTeamLocked): SwapController moves no pad, except
# that a pad the goalie borrowed to throw the ball out goes back to the fielder
# it belongs to.
